"expect-only: not-callable"
"`(-1 2)` is a call whose callee is the number -1, because a sign binds to the"
"digits after it. Written with a space, `(- 1 2)` is subtraction; written"
"without, it is this. Both backends only discover it at compile time — a"
"TypeError from Python, E0618 from rustc — so the checker names it instead."
(defun difference [] -> Int64
  :doc "Subtraction, misspelt as an application of a literal."
  (-1 2))
